      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{p(5p-2)}{6(3p+8)}$ for $p=-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $p$ with $-3$ in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{p(5p-2)}{6(3p+8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{(-3)(5(-3)-2)}{6(3(-3)+8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{(-3)(-15-2)}{6(-9+8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{(-3)(-17)}{6(-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{51}{(-6)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
